# Flight booking — travel document (DNI / passport) data

Applies when collecting government ID for Duffel order creation. This is more sensitive than other BeTacora data. **Legal review is required before shipping any ID-collection UI or API.**

## Default: do not persist

- Prefer sending passport/DNI fields **directly to Duffel** in the order-create request only.
- Do **not** write full document numbers, issue/expiry dates, nationality pages, or scans to Supabase (or logs, analytics, Sentry breadcrumbs, etc.) unless strictly required.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — memory → Duffel only
await duffel.orders.create({ ...passengersWithDocuments });

// ❌ BAD — plaintext ID in our DB
await supabase.from("passengers").insert({ passport_number: raw });
```

## If temporary storage is unavoidable

Only while a booking is in flight (e.g. multi-step checkout, webhook retry):

1. **Encrypt at rest** (app-level encryption before insert; never store plaintext columns).
2. **Restrict access** — service role / narrow RLS; no client read of ciphertext or plaintext.
3. **Auto-delete** soon after success **or** failure (short TTL, e.g. hours not days). Prefer scheduled purge + delete-on-terminal-status.
4. Store at most a **masked** display form if the UI needs a reminder (`***4567`), never the full number after submit.

```ts
// ✅ Mask for UI after submit
function maskDoc(n: string) {
  const digits = n.replace(/\s/g, "");
  return "***" + digits.slice(-4);
}
```

## UI

- Never show the full DNI/passport number again after it has been submitted/saved.
- Do not echo full IDs in emails, itinerary HTML, or share cards.

## Out of scope today

Search/select flows (`searchFlights`, `/api/duffel/search-offers`, `/api/flights/select`) must stay **offer-only** — no travel-document fields on those payloads.
